01:15:22,500 --> 01:15:28,500
The Swimmers is a 2022 biographical sports drama film directed by Sally
El Hosaini, who co-wrote the screenplay with Jack Thorne.

10
01:23:45,000 --> 01:23:51,000
The film stars real-life sisters Nathalie Issa and Manal Issa, Ahmed Malek, Matthias
Schweighöfer, Ali Suliman, Kinda Alloush, James Krishna Floyd, and Elmi Rashid Elmi.

11
01:32:07,500 --> 01:32:13,500
The film follows two young sisters who embark on a risky voyage from war-torn Syria to Rio
de Janeiro, Brazil, as one of them competes in the 2016 Summer Olympics.

12
01:40:30,000 --> 01:40:36,000
The Swimmers premiered at the 2022 Toronto International Film Festival on September 8, 2022, and was
released in select cinemas on November 11 before its streaming release on November 23, by Netflix.

13
01:48:52,500 --> 01:48:58,500
The film was nominated at the 2023 BAFTA film awards for Outstanding British Film, received positive reviews from
critics and was a global hit on Netflix, achieving no.1 in 15 countries and top 10 in 85 countries.

14
01:57:15,000 --> 01:57:21,000
The film explores themes of refugee, olympian sports team,
biography, based on true story, family relationships.

15
02:05:37,500 --> 02:05:43,500
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
